| Feature | WebGPU | WASM CPU Inference |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Performance** | Hardware-accelerated via GPU, enabling parallel processing for massive matrix operations. | Limited by single-threaded CPU cores, resulting in lower throughput for large models. |
| **Latency** | Lower latency due to optimized native GPU kernels and asynchronous execution. | Higher latency caused by interpreter overhead and lack of parallelism. |

```javascript
// Example: Pseudo-code for a WebGPU compute shader vs WASM loop
// WebGPU: Uses compute shaders for parallel matrix multiplication
// WASM: Uses a JavaScript loop for sequential scalar operations

// WebGPU Compute Shader (Conceptual)
// @compute 128
// @group(0)
// @binding(0)
// @binding(1)
fn matMul(out: vec4, a: mat4, b: mat4) {
    out = mat4Mul(out, a, b); // GPU handles parallelization
}

